From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:15:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] Multithreaded engine: opt-in tiled sweep, several
 timesteps per pass over one shared tile (snapshot cg32d)

Off by default. OPENEMS_TBLOCK=k (or auto) runs k timesteps on one tile of
x-lines before moving on, with every thread working in the same tile (its
share of the y lines), so a tile is read from memory once per k timesteps.
The design follows the cpu engine of upstream master (one cache-sized tile
shared by all threads); none of its code is used.

- engine_sse_compressed: the IJKN update loops take a y range
  (UpdateVoltagesY / UpdateCurrentsY).
- engine_multithread: SetupTiled builds the task list per block depth
  (trapezoids along x, then the wedges between tiles); TiledRun runs it with
  one spin barrier per task. Line hooks run in stages between two updates,
  on all threads: the x-lines of a stage are cut once into one share per
  thread, so every hook of an x-line (and of the pairs 0|1 and NX-2|NX-1)
  runs on one thread in the one-thread order. No extension was changed for
  this; it relies on the line hook contract in engine_extension.h.
- Shares follow each thread's measured update speed (BalanceTiled; at least
  one y line per thread; OPENEMS_BALANCE=0 keeps them equal).
- OPENEMS_TBLOCK=auto: the deepest k <= 8 whose tile of 2k+1 x-lines stays
  within 90 % of the cache the threads share (hw.perflevel0.l2cachesize on
  macOS, sysconf L3/L2 elsewhere); no tiling when the fields fit that cache
  or two timesteps of a tile do not. OPENEMS_TBLOCK_W sets the tile width,
  OPENEMS_TBLOCK_HOOKS=0 runs the hook stages on one thread (diagnostic).
- Refused, with a message: an extension that is not TS_LOCAL, coupled lines
  other than 0 and NX-2, fewer x-lines than two tiles.
- Engine_Extension::GetMaxBlockDepth() (default: no limit) caps the depth;
  the steady-state extension returns one signal period.

Checked bit-identical to the fused sweep of ff2538a on an Apple M5 (probes
of six models at 1 to 10 threads, depths 2 to 8 and auto, hooks and balance
on and off; raw fields of a closed cylinder and of a steady-state box that
stops by its criterion at the same step; Debye box), and with the variable
unset on the six models against stock v0.37.0.

Not measured yet: its speed on a quiet machine. Under heavy load from other
programs the barrier per task made it much slower than the fused sweep at
8 to 10 threads, which is why it stays opt-in.

